# Firebase web configuration.
#
# These values are PUBLIC by design and ship in the built bundle. The `apiKey`
# identifies the Firebase project; it does not authorise anything. They live here
# for environment separation (dev project vs prod project), NOT for secrecy.
#
# What actually protects the project:
#   - firestore.rules            (the only server-side check this app has)
#   - Firebase authorised domains (Authentication → Settings)
#   - an HTTP-referrer restriction on the browser key, in the Google Cloud console
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in from:
#   Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps → Web app → SDK setup and configuration
#
# Leaving these unset is supported: the app runs signed-out only and never offers
# sign-in. That is also what CI does.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
